Create a function that takes in three parameters: the class name of the elements to change, the new color to change them to, and the duration of the color transition animation in milliseconds. The function should change the background color of all elements with the given class name to the specified new color over the specified duration.

Additionally, if the class name starts with "animate-", the function should also add a CSS animation effect to the elements with the specified duration and delay. The CSS animation effect should be a rotating animation with a duration of 1 second and a linear timing function.

If the new color is not a valid CSS color value, the function should throw an error.

### Response:
Here is a possible implementation of the function:

```javascript
function changeElementColor(className, newColor, duration) {
  const elements = document.getElementsByClassName(className);

  if (!elements.length) {
    console.log(`No elements found with class name: ${className}`);
    return;
  }

  // Check if newColor is a valid CSS color value
  const isValidColor = /^#[0-9A-F]{6}$/i.test(newColor);
  if (!isValidColor) {
    throw new Error(`Invalid CSS color value: ${newColor}`);
  }

  // Set the background color and transition duration for all elements
  for (let i = 0; i < elements.length; i++) {
    elements[i].style.backgroundColor = newColor;
    elements[i].style.transitionDuration = `${duration}ms`;
  }

  // Add animation effect if class name starts with "animate-"
  if (className.startsWith("animate-")) {
    for (let i = 0; i < elements.length; i++) {
      elements[i].style.animation = `rotation ${duration}ms linear`;
    }
  }
}
```

