Write a Java class named "Shape" which has an abstract method named "surfaceArea". Additionally, the "Shape" class should have a constructor that takes in a parameter representing the dimensions of the shape. The dimensions can be of any type, such as integers or floating-point numbers. The "Shape" class should also have a method named "volume" which calculates and returns the volume of the shape based on its dimensions. The volume calculation should be specific to each type of shape (e.g., a cube would have a different volume calculation compared to a sphere). 

Create three subclasses of the "Shape" class: "Cube", "Sphere", and "Cylinder". Each subclass should implement the "surfaceArea" and "volume" methods based on their specific shape type. 

The "Cube" subclass should have an additional method called "isPerfectCube" which checks if the given shape is a perfect cube, meaning that all sides have equal length.

The "Sphere" subclass should have an additional method called "isHollow" which checks if the given sphere is hollow, meaning that it has a non-zero thickness for the outer shell.

The "Cylinder" subclass should have an additional method called "calculateLateralSurfaceArea" which calculates and returns the lateral surface area of the cylinder, excluding the top and bottom bases.

### Response:
Here is the implementation of the "Shape" class and its subclasses:

```java
abstract class Shape {
    private Object dimensions;

    public Shape(Object dimensions) {
        this.dimensions = dimensions;
    }

    public abstract double surfaceArea();

    public abstract double volume();

    public Object getDimensions() {
        return dimensions;
    }
}

class Cube extends Shape {
    public Cube(double sideLength) {
        super(sideLength);
    }

    public boolean isPerfectCube() {
        double sideLength = (double) getDimensions();
        return sideLength > 0 && (int) sideLength == sideLength;
    }

    @Override
    public double surfaceArea() {
        double sideLength = (double) getDimensions();
        return 6 * sideLength * sideLength;
    }

    @Override
    public double volume() {
        double sideLength = (double) getDimensions();
        return sideLength * sideLength * sideLength;
    }
}

class Sphere extends Shape {
    public Sphere(double radius) {
        super(radius);
    }

    public boolean isHollow() {
        double radius = (double) getDimensions();
        return radius > 0;
    }

    @Override
    public double surfaceArea() {
        double radius = (double) getDimensions();
        return 4 * Math.PI * radius * radius;
    }

    @Override
    public double volume() {
        double radius = (double) getDimensions();
        return (4.0 / 3.0) * Math.PI * radius * radius * radius;
    }
}

class Cylinder extends Shape {
    private double height;

    public Cylinder(double radius, double height) {
        super(radius);
        this.height = height;
    }

    public double getHeight() {
        return height;
    }

    public double calculateLateralSurfaceArea() {
        double radius = (double) getDimensions();
        return 2 * Math.PI * radius * height;
    }

    @Override
    public double surfaceArea() {
        double radius = (double) getDimensions();
        return 2 * Math.PI * radius * (radius + height);
    }

    @Override
    public double volume() {
        double radius = (double) getDimensions();
        return Math.PI * radius * radius * height;
    }
}
```

