### Instruction:
Create a Java program for finding the first non-repeated character in a string, while ignoring any whitespace characters. The string may contain special characters and numbers. The program should have a time complexity of O(n) and should not use any additional data structures. 

String: hello 123&@^# world

### Response:
Here's a Java program that finds the first non-repeated character in a string while ignoring whitespace characters:

```java
public class FirstNonRepeatedCharacter {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String inputString = "hello 123&@^# world";
        char firstNonRepeatedChar = findFirstNonRepeatedChar(inputString);
        System.out.println("First non-repeated character: " + firstNonRepeatedChar);
    }

    public static char findFirstNonRepeatedChar(String inputString) {
        int[] charCount = new int[256]; // Assuming ASCII character set

        // Count occurrences of each character
        for (int i = 0; i < inputString.length(); i++) {
            char c = inputString.charAt(i);
            if (c == ' ') continue; // Ignore whitespace characters
            charCount[c]++;
        }

        // Find the first non-repeated character
        for (int i = 0; i < inputString.length(); i++) {
            char c = inputString.charAt(i);
            if (c == ' ') continue; // Ignore whitespace characters
            if (charCount[c] == 1) {
                return c;
            }
        }

        return '\0'; // Return null character if no non-repeated character found
    }
}
```

This program uses an integer array `charCount` of size 256 to count the occurrences of each character in the input string. It then iterates over the input string to find the first non-repeated character by checking the count of each character. The time complexity of this program is O(n), where n is the length of the input string, as it iterates over the string twice.

